=== [A2] multi-target: distinct salt prefixes vs shared-salt positive control ===
    * DISTINCT-salt  (the real construction): predict cost flat in T ~ 2^{n0}
    * SHARED-salt    (control, same IV):       predict cost ~ 2^{n0}/T  (real /T)
        T |   DISTINCT log2(calls) |  SHARED(control) log2(calls)
      -> DISTINCT slope d log2(calls)/d log2(T) = -0.15   (predict 0 = NO multi-target speedup)
      -> SHARED   slope d log2(calls)/d log2(T) = -1.10   (predict -1 = real /T; proves the harness can see a speedup)
        T |   DISTINCT log2(calls) |  SHARED(control) log2(calls)
      -> DISTINCT slope d log2(calls)/d log2(T) = +0.05   (predict 0 = NO multi-target speedup)
      -> SHARED   slope d log2(calls)/d log2(T) = -1.25   (predict -1 = real /T; proves the harness can see a speedup)

